Spirit of the liscense
In the history of computing - there have been many other Operating Systems -
Almost universally, an Operating System and the software built around it - 
Will conform to atleast "A" set of standards.

This is termed heritage, or lineage, a common ancestry, "Genetic unix"

These operating systems share actual source code, descending from and tracing back to the original AT&T Bell Labs Unix.

The development of Unix wasn't driven by corporate milestones, market research, or profit margins. 

Instead - It was driven by peer respect and the joy of creation.
In a culture of continuous, playful iteration.

The nature of unix-like and posix software "is" - that shared heritage.

